Here is a very good example how line numbers doesn't actually help at 
all while trying to find out typing errors in C code.

For a new coder one of the typical errors is missing a closing brace. So 
I duplicated this by removing a closing brace from line 40 in the file 
allmain.c of NetHack.

My compiler reported two errors:

error C2143: syntax error : missing ';' before 'type' on line 430
error C2059: syntax error : '}' on line 445

So the line numbers aren't even very helpfull except that now we know 
that there is a problem somwhere before line 430.

